Looking at the `read` implementation in receive.c, I notice it allocates a buffer, calls `recvmsg_wrapper` to read data, then checks the result. The problem is that if `recvmsg_wrapper` times out and the poll indicates no data is available, the native code might not be propagating the timeout exception up to Java before returning -1.

