Looking at the poll logic itself, when `millis == 0`, the function should return 1 for a blocking socket, but on OpenBSD it loops polling until data arrives. However, when a non-zero timeout is set and the poll completes, the native code needs to handle the return value correctly—it should return 0 if the poll timed out or -1 on error, not continue with the buffer allocation.

